    {
      "id": "43b05741-da1f-4828-910d-91651281c327",
      "url": "https://jamesclear.com/atomic-habits",
      "text": "Atomic Habits — tiny changes, remarkable results.",
      "imageUrl": "",
      "avatarUrl": "",
      "authorName": "James Clear",
      "authorHandle": "",
      "siteName": "jamesclear.com",
      "articleText": "You do not rise to the level of your goals. You fall to the level of your systems. Habits are the compound interest of self-improvement.\n\nThe four laws: make it obvious, make it attractive, make it easy, and make it satisfying. Invert them to break a bad habit.",
      "fetched": true,
      "enrichAttempts": 0,
      "spaceId": "a92ea55c-6391-4e41-9047-49c997fb3d74",
      "pinned": false,
      "archived": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "noteTitle": "Habits worth stealing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "072e333c-576e-462f-8818-eb915d642260",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two ideas I keep coming back to: make it obvious, make it easy. The two-minute rule is the one that actually changed my mornings. Pairs well with [[On slow mornings]].",
          "imagePath": ""
        }
      ],
